            <div xml:id="d757">

                <pb facs="0723" n="711" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg711"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A Passenger Travel/42: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-11-22T20:00:00-05:00">November 22,
                            1939—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1433. Your 2799, November 21, 6 p.m. Presidential Proclamation so far limits
                    combat areas to water. Countries bordering on waters described as combat areas
                    are not themselves combat areas.</p>
                <p>Telegraphic circular instruction regarding validation of passports of Americans
                    in Europe dispatched Berne today.<anchor n="73" xml:id="d757-f1"/> It is
                    believed this circular covers second point your telegram.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
